## 3. Darren Roblyer, PhD
**Professor (BME, ECE affiliate); Associate Chair for Graduate Studies, BME; Director, Biomedical Optical Technologies Lab (BOTLab)**

**Summary:** Works on translational diffuse optical spectroscopy and imaging using near-infrared light. His lab builds wearable optical probes, including a wearable probe for cuffless blood pressure using speckle contrast optical spectroscopy (SCOS), a wearable SWIR hydration probe, and flexible probes for monitoring breast cancer treatment.

**Relevance to MHRS:** Probably the closest match to the project. His lab has iterated on wearable LED/photodiode probes, from early rigid single-source designs to flexible arrays. That experience covers optical coupling, probe geometry, ambient-light rejection, and continuous monitoring of microvascular blood flow during daily activity, which maps onto your housing/geometry and motion-robustness goals.

**Contact:**
- Email: roblyer@bu.edu
- Lab: https://www.bu.edu/botlab

